 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The prediction for each sample involves $2^n - 1$ lookups and additions. The traversal is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the total number of samples.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** The memory footprint is $O(\prod_{i=1}^{n-1} D_i)$, which is the size of the largest slice plus lower-dimensional footprints. This is much smaller than the full dataset $O(\prod_{i=1}^{n} D_i)$, making it suitable for out-of-core processing [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** The prediction for each sample involves $2^n - 1$ lookups and additions. The traversal is linear in the number of samples $N$. Thus, time complexity is $O(N \cdot 2^n)$.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** The memory footprint is proportional to the size of the footprint buffer, which is $O(\prod_{i=1}^{n-1} D_i)$. This is significantly smaller than storing the entire dataset, making it suitable for out-of-core processing [S1, unofficial].
